{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UJWP4M75ExNtfitFBiQ9WB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Codebase perspective on metrics format","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:codebase-analyst","prompt":"You are resolving an ambiguous clarify question from a SpecKit workflow. Provide the codebase perspective only — do not synthesize across other viewpoints.\n\nQuestion (Q1): Should the new metrics emitter use Prometheus exposition format or OpenTelemetry OTLP?\n\nYour job: search the current repository for established patterns and conventions that would inform this choice. Specifically look for:\n- Existing metrics, telemetry, or observability code (collectors, exporters, emitters)\n- Dependencies in package manifests (package.json, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml, go.mod, Cargo.toml, etc.) that reference Prometheus, OpenTelemetry, OTLP, prom-client, opentelemetry-sdk, etc.\n- Configuration files referencing scrape endpoints, OTLP collectors, /metrics routes, or telemetry exporters\n- CI/CD or deployment manifests (Helm charts, Docker Compose, k8s manifests) that wire up a metrics backend\n- Constitution, ADRs, or <PATH> under docs/ that prescribe an observability stack\n- Prior spec artifacts under specs/ or .specify/ that already chose one format\n\nReturn a structured answer:\n1. **Codebase recommendation:** Prometheus | OTLP | no established pattern\n2. **File-level evidence:** list specific paths + line numbers supporting the recommendation\n3. **Conflicts:** any places where both stacks appear or contradict\n4. **Confidence:** high | medium | low, with reasoning\n\nIf there is no established pattern in the codebase, say so plainly — do not invent one. Keep the response under 400 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
