{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UbtMEgra6Qw82Ym3JqUgxV","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Domain research on metrics format","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:domain-researcher","prompt":"You are resolving an ambiguous clarify question from a SpecKit workflow. Provide the industry/domain perspective only — do not synthesize across other viewpoints.\n\nQuestion (Q1): Should the new metrics emitter use Prometheus exposition format or OpenTelemetry OTLP?\n\nYour job: research current industry best practices and official documentation to recommend a format choice on its merits, independent of this codebase. Use Tavily, Context7, and WebSearch to ground your answer in primary sources from:\n- CNCF / OpenTelemetry project documentation (otel-spec, OTEP proposals)\n- Prometheus project documentation (exposition formats, OpenMetrics relationship)\n- Cloud vendor guidance (AWS, GCP, Azure observability stacks)\n- Recent (2024-2026) community guidance on Prometheus vs OTLP tradeoffs\n- The current state of Prometheus native OTLP ingestion support\n\nReturn a structured answer:\n1. **Domain recommendation:** Prometheus exposition | OTLP | depends-on-X (state X)\n2. **Evidence:** cite 3-5 authoritative sources with URLs and a one-line summary of each\n3. **Key tradeoffs:** push vs pull, ecosystem maturity, vendor lock-in, migration cost, current convergence trends\n4. **Confidence:** high | medium | low, with reasoning\n\nBe honest about ambiguity in the industry — if both formats are defensible defaults for different scenarios, name the scenarios. Keep the response under 500 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
